  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "If $U={-20,-19,-18,\u2026,20}$ is the universal set and $A={1,2,3,\u2026,20},$ then $\\overset{\u2015}{A}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integers $-20$ through $20,$ while he set $A$ consists of the integers $1$ through $28.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the integers $-20$ through $0.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{A}={-20,-19,-18,\u2026,0}.\n$$",
